# Chroma library, modern Earth: aims v1, group D (R, R G and R W faces): the spark moments of earth_aims.py.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Build: python3 build.py earth_aim_moments. Nothing reads it until the Engine's aims switch is on.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to see the world (R), spark; cycle s1

== a ticket bought on a whim
tier: life event
aim: to see the world
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-65
per_year: 0 0 .5 .4 .3 0
times: While the aim is set, a cheap far-off ticket within reach comes most years in the young years, less often later (estimate)
gap: 1-4
tone: joy
life: travel, leisure
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent
earth: a cheap ticket to a city across the sea, bought at midnight with money meant for something else
tribal: a band of traders heading past the far hills offers a place on the walk
magic: a caravan leaving for the far realm has one seat left on the last wagon
scene: At midnight {N} buys a cheap ticket to a city on the far side of the sea, with money meant for something sensible. The flight is on Friday. {parent} thinks it is madness, and {friend} wants to come.
scene W: {N} has never gone anywhere without telling everyone first, and does not mean to start now.
scene U: {N} already has the city's map open, and the names of its streets are strange and wonderful.
scene B: The ticket was a bargain. {N} wonders, a little, what it would fetch on Thursday.
scene R: {Ns} heart has not slowed since the button was pressed. Friday cannot come fast enough.
scene G: Somewhere over there are cousins nobody has visited in two generations.
- W | tell everyone the plan and promise to ring home every night | v: security, benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U | read up on the place at the library every evening until Friday | v: self-direction | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 90
- B | sell the ticket on at a profit and keep the money | v: achievement | dream: drop | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 75
- R | go alone, with one bag and no plan past the first night | v: stimulation, self-direction | dream: test | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 70
- G | go to the town the grandparents left, and find the cousins who stayed | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 70
- W>U | sign up for an evening class in the language before the flight | v: conformity, self-direction | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 80
- U>B | work out how to make the money stretch to three weeks instead of one | v: security, achievement | foot: lesson every coin can go further | chance: 70
- B>R | pick up casual work out there and stay a month longer than planned | v: achievement, stimulation | foot: means freedom+.06 | chance: 60
- R>G | leave the tourist trail and stay with a family in a hill village | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- G>W | bring back a small gift for every house on the street | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
works: {N} comes home sunburnt, with a head full of streets and a list of places still to go.
works: The trip is everything {N} hoped, and the first night back {N} is already looking at the departure board.
fails: The trip is cut short by a lost bag and a fever, and {N} comes home early and flat.
fails: The city is grey and expensive, and {N} spends most of the week wishing to be somewhere else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to love with everything (R), spark; cycle s2

== saying it first
tier: life event
aim: to love with everything
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 16-65
per_year: 0 0 .5 .4 .3 0
times: While the aim is set and someone new is close, the moment to say it first comes once in most such loves (estimate)
gap: 1-5
tone: mixed
life: love
horizon: months
roles: prospect, friend, grandparent
earth: three months into something new, and the words are right there
tribal: the one {N} has watched across the fire all season is leaving with their band at dawn
magic: at the guild's ball, the one {N} cannot stop thinking of is leaving for a far tower in the morning
scene: Three months of long walks and late calls, and {N} is sure. Tonight, on the bridge, with {prospect} talking about something else entirely, the words are right there.
scene W: {N} has always thought some things should be said properly, at the right time and in the right place.
scene B: Whoever says it first has shown their hand. {N} has never liked showing a hand.
scene R: {N} has never been able to hold a feeling in for long, and this one is the biggest yet.
scene G: {N} keeps thinking of the old couple next door, still holding hands at the bus stop.
- W | wait until after meeting their family, and then say it properly | v: tradition, conformity | foot: lesson love can wait a little | chance: 80
- U | write it all in a letter and leave it in their coat pocket | v: self-direction | foot: person prospect | chance: 70
- B | wait for them to say it first, however long it takes | v: security, power | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 75
- R | say it now, on the bridge, loud enough for the whole river to hear | v: stimulation, hedonism | dream: test | foot: person prospect; mark took a wild risk | chance: 70
- G | bring them home for a long Sunday lunch with everyone | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- W>B | ask them plainly whether they mean to stay in town | v: security, achievement | foot: lesson ask plainly and know | chance: 75
- U>R | plan a whole surprise day out of every small thing they ever loved | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 70
- B>G | keep the feeling to yourself, and keep the friendship safe | v: security | dream: drop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
- R>W | propose a summer away together, and mean it for good | v: stimulation, benevolence | dream: seal | foot: person prospect; door kept your word | chance: 60
- G>U | ask the old couple next door how they knew, all those years ago | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
works: {prospect} laughs, then goes quiet, and says it back, and the night goes on for a very long time.
works: Whatever {N} did, it lands; by the end of the week everyone who matters knows they are together.
fails: {prospect} is kind about it, and careful, and {N} walks home knowing it was not the same for both of them.
fails: The moment passes, the summer passes, and the words are still unsaid when {prospect} moves away.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to stand up for the underdog (R), spark; cycle s3

== the shouting in the queue
tier: life event
aim: to stand up for the underdog
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile+
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .4 .5 .4 .3 .3
times: While the aim is set, seeing someone pushed about in public, and having the chance to step in, comes every year or two (estimate)
gap: 1-3
tone: trouble
life: strangers, justice
horizon: moment
roles: neighbour, a stranger, the regulars
earth: in the queue at the post office, a man is shouting at an old woman who cannot read the form
tribal: at the waterhole a big hunter shoves an old widow out of the line, and nobody moves
magic: in the market a guild bully kicks a hedge-witch's basket into the gutter, and the crowd looks away
scene: The queue at the post office is long and hot. At the front, a big man is shouting at an old woman who cannot read the form, and everyone has found something interesting to look at on the floor.
scene W: There are rules for a queue, and none of them says a man may shout at a frightened old woman.
scene U: {N} notices the clerk behind the glass, pretending not to hear, and the man's car left across the doorway outside.
scene B: {N} is third in line and in a hurry. Getting involved would cost the afternoon.
scene R: Something hot rises in {N}. It always does, when someone smaller is pushed about.
scene G: {N} thinks the woman might be from the flats behind the church, where {Ns} own grandmother lived.
- W | call the manager over and ask for the queue's rules to be kept | v: conformity, universalism | foot: person keeper | chance: 75
- U | film the man quietly, in case it ends in a complaint | v: security | foot: lesson a record speaks later | chance: 85
- B | let it play out, and keep your place in the line | v: security, power | dream: drop | foot: door refused someone in need | chance: 90
- R | step between them and tell him to stop, now | v: benevolence, stimulation | dream: test | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 65
- G | stand beside the woman so she is not alone, and help her with the form | v: benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- W>R | get the whole queue to say together that enough is enough | v: universalism, stimulation | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 60
- U>G | find out afterwards who she is, and look in on her next week | v: benevolence | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 80
- B>W | have a quiet word at the counter and get him barred from the place | v: power, conformity | foot: lesson the right ear matters | chance: 65
- R>U | ask him loudly, in front of everyone, what exactly she has done to him | v: stimulation, universalism | dream: test | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- G>B | ask the regulars to walk her home, and keep an eye on him | v: benevolence, security | foot: person regular | chance: 80
works: The man goes quiet, then goes, and the old woman holds on to {Ns} arm a moment longer than she needs to.
works: The queue comes back to life, people start talking to each other, and someone pats {N} on the shoulder on the way out.
fails: The man turns on {N} instead, and the whole queue watches it happen and does nothing.
fails: The old woman leaves in tears before anyone can stop her, and {N} cannot shake it for days.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to feel something greater in the music (R), spark; cycle s4

== the night the singing lifts the roof
tier: life event
aim: to feel something greater in the music
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile+
age: 12-95
per_year: 0 .4 .4 .4 .4 .4
times: While the aim is set, a gathering where a whole room sings comes a few times a year to those who go (estimate)
gap: .5-2
tone: joy
life: faith, music
horizon: moment
roles: elder, friend, grandparent
earth: at the midwinter service the old hymn starts, and the whole packed hall is singing
tribal: the drums go on past midnight at the gathering, and the dancers circle the fire
magic: in the old temple the chant rises, and the stones seem to hum with it
scene: The hall is packed for the midwinter service, and when the old hymn starts the whole room is singing. Something rises in {N}, in the chest and the throat, that has no name.
scene W: The words are on the sheet, and {N} has known them since childhood. Tonight they sound new.
scene U: {N} has always wondered what the old words actually mean, and why they move people so.
scene B: {N} came because {friend} asked, and keeps one eye on the clock.
scene R: The sound goes right through {N}, like standing too close to the sea.
scene G: {Ns} grandmother sang this one every winter, a little flat and very loud.
- W | sing every verse as written, standing with the whole congregation | v: tradition, conformity | foot: place faith.congregation | chance: 90
- U | listen hard for what the old words are really saying | v: self-direction | foot: place faith.seeking | chance: 85
- B | slip out before the collection comes round | v: security, hedonism | dream: drop | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 90
- R | close your eyes and sing out, with everything there is | v: stimulation, hedonism | dream: test | foot: place arts.song | chance: 80
- G | sing the harmony the grandmother used to sing, word for word | v: tradition | foot: lesson the old songs still carry | chance: 85
- W>G | ask the choir leader if there is room for one more voice | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- U>W | stay behind to ask the organist where the old tune came from | v: self-direction, tradition | foot: person elder | chance: 85
- B>U | record the singing on a phone to learn the harmony at home | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- R>B | dance in the aisle until the young ones start to join in | v: stimulation, hedonism | dream: test | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- G>R | stamp and clap the beat the old way, until the whole row is clapping | v: tradition, stimulation | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
works: For a few minutes {N} is not one person but part of the sound, and walks out into the frost lit up from inside.
works: The last chord hangs in the rafters, and {N} knows, without words for it, that this will be sought again.
fails: {N} tries to feel it and feels only tired, and a little foolish, among all those raised voices.
fails: The moment is broken by a cough, a phone and a crying baby, and it never comes back that night.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to live wild and free outdoors (R G), spark; cycle s1

== the first night alone on the hill
tier: life event
aim: to live wild and free outdoors
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 14-70
per_year: 0 .4 .5 .4 .3 0
times: While the aim is set, the chance to spend a night out alone in wild country comes most years (estimate)
gap: 1-3
tone: mixed
life: nature, leisure
horizon: week
roles: friend, parent, mentor
earth: a tent, a map and a hill nobody else is walking, with rain coming in from the west
tribal: the young ones are sent alone past the river to spend a night in the wild and come back changed
magic: the old forest past the last tower is said to keep travellers, and {N} goes in alone
scene: {N} has walked up past the last farm with a small tent and a map, meaning to sleep out alone for the first time. The light is going, and there is rain coming in from the west.
scene W: {N} told {parent} exactly where, and when, and means to keep to it.
scene U: {N} has studied the map for a week and knows every contour, but not yet the feel of the ground.
scene B: This is a test, and {N} intends to pass it, whatever it takes.
scene R: There is nobody for miles. {N} has never felt so free, or so small.
scene G: The hill has been here for ever, and {N} feels, for once, that it does not mind the company.
- W | leave a note of the route and the hour to be back by | v: security, conformity | foot: door kept your word | chance: 90
- U | learn the stars and the map well enough to need neither | v: self-direction | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | turn back at the first rain, and call it a good walk | v: security | dream: drop | foot: lesson the hill will still be there | chance: 92
- R | go on past the last path and sleep wherever the dark comes down | v: stimulation, self-direction | dream: test | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 65
- G | build a shelter of branches, the old way, and stay three nights | v: tradition, self-direction | dream: test | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 65
- W>U | go to the mountain rescue's open day and learn the ropes first | v: conformity, security | foot: place prot.rescue | chance: 85
- U>B | test new kit on the hill and write it up for the outdoor shop | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 70
- B>R | bet a friend a week out there alone is easy | v: stimulation, achievement | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R>G | follow the deer trail up to the high tarn and swim at dawn | v: stimulation, hedonism | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 75
- G>W | walk out with the old shepherd who knows every fold of the hill | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person mentor | chance: 85
works: {N} wakes at dawn to mist in the valley below and a hare sitting ten feet away, and walks home a different person.
works: The rain comes and goes, the tent holds, and {N} comes down the hill already planning the next one.
fails: The tent leaks, the cold gets in, and {N} trudges home before midnight, wet through and cross.
fails: {N} gets lost in the cloud and has to ring for help, and the walk home is a long and quiet one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to raise a big, loud family (R G), spark; cycle s2

== a whole weekend of other people's children
tier: life event
aim: to raise a big, loud family
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-50
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 0 0
times: While the aim is set, a weekend with a house full of nieces, nephews or the neighbours' children comes most years (estimate)
gap: 1-3
tone: joy
life: family, home
horizon: week
roles: sibling, neighbour, partner
earth: the cousins' three and two of the neighbours' children stay the whole weekend, and the house is chaos
tribal: the families go out to the hunt, and every child of the camp is left at {Ns} fire for two days
magic: the lane's families go to the fair, and every child in the lane ends up in {Ns} kitchen
scene: {sibling}'s three are staying the whole weekend, and by Saturday lunchtime two of the neighbours' children have joined them. There are shoes on the stairs, a dog under the table and somebody crying in the garden.
scene W: {N} believes children are happiest with rules they can count on, and has written some down.
scene U: {N} looks at five children and sees five little engineers waiting for a project.
scene B: {N} loves them all, and also has plans for Sunday afternoon.
scene R: The noise is enormous. {N} has never been happier.
scene G: This is how a house should sound, {N} thinks: full, and loud, and alive.
- W | set bedtimes, chores and a rota on the fridge, and keep to it | v: conformity, security | foot: lesson children like knowing the rules | chance: 75
- U | turn the weekend into one big building project with a job for every child | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 75
- B | pay the teenager next door to take them all to the park for a day | v: hedonism | dream: drop | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 90
- R | build a den of every cushion in the house and lead a pillow war | v: stimulation, hedonism | dream: test | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- G | cook one huge pot of stew and sit everyone round the one table | v: benevolence, tradition | dream: test | foot: place gather.house | chance: 80
- W>B | agree a fixed handover time with the parents, and hold them to it | v: security, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U>R | invent a treasure hunt that runs the length of the street | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person neighbour | chance: 80
- B>G | set up a weekend swap with the other parents, so the favour comes back | v: security, benevolence | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 80
- R>W | march the whole gang to the park and referee their match | v: stimulation, conformity | foot: place gather.games | chance: 80
- G>U | let the oldest teach the youngest how to bake the family bread | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: lesson children teach each other best | chance: 85
works: By Sunday night the house is wrecked and quiet, and {N} sits on the stairs grinning at the mess.
works: The children beg to come back next weekend, and {sibling} says {N} has spoiled them for anywhere else.
fails: By Saturday night there are two fights, one broken window and a headache that lasts until Tuesday.
fails: The weekend is long and loud and joyless, and {N} wonders, for the first time, whether a houseful is really the dream.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to dance (R G), spark; cycle s3

== the empty floor at the wedding
tier: life event
aim: to dance
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile+
age: 12-85
per_year: 0 .4 .5 .4 .3 .3
times: While the aim is set, a wedding, party or gathering with music and an empty floor comes a few times a year (estimate)
gap: .5-2
tone: joy
life: celebration, music
horizon: moment
roles: friend, elder, a band
earth: at a cousin's wedding the band strikes up and the floor stays empty, everyone waiting for someone else
tribal: the drums start at the summer gathering, and the whole circle waits for the first dancer
magic: at the harvest ball the fiddlers begin, and the whole hall waits for someone to step out
scene: At a cousin's wedding the band strikes up an old song everybody knows, and the floor stays empty. A hundred people sit with their drinks, each waiting for somebody else to go first.
scene W: There is an order to these things: the couple first, then the families, then everyone else.
scene U: {N} has been watching one old woman's feet under the table, keeping a step {N} has never seen.
scene B: {N} knows exactly how foolish the first dancer will look. It will not be {N}.
scene R: The music gets into {Ns} legs and will not leave.
scene G: The song is one the whole family dances to, and the old ones are already tapping their feet.
