- R>U | dance with every stranger on the floor, one song each | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G>B | get the cousins up in a line to show the room how it is done | v: tradition, power | foot: lesson a family dances best together | chance: 75
works: The floor fills behind {N} in a single song, and the dancing goes on until the band packs up.
works: Someone {N} has never met says it was the best thing at the whole wedding, and {N} cannot stop smiling.
fails: {N} dances one song alone, flushed and awkward, and sits down to a ripple of polite applause.
fails: The band switches to something slow before anyone is up, and the moment passes.

