scene W: There must be a proper way to object, {N} thinks, and a date by which to do it.
scene U: {N} has seen owls in this wood, and orchids by the stream. Somebody must have written that down.
scene B: Land like this is worth a fortune with a car park on it. {N} cannot help doing the sums.
scene R: The thought of the old oak coming down makes {N} want to shout at somebody.
scene G: The wood was here before the town, and {N} has always thought it would be here after.
