works: The diggers come on Saturday and go away again, and by spring the plan is quietly withdrawn.
works: The wood is saved, or half of it, and {N} walks the path on Sunday knowing which half and why.
fails: The diggers come anyway, and by Monday evening there is mud and a fence where the wood was.
