tone: trouble
life: work, justice
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, elder
earth: a colleague who complained about a broken ladder is let go on a Friday afternoon, and everyone knows why
tribal: the headman has cast out a young hunter for speaking against him at the council fire
magic: the guildmaster has struck a journeyman from the rolls for reporting a rotten beam
scene: On Friday afternoon {colleague}, who complained twice about the broken ladder in the stockroom, is called upstairs and let go. On Monday the ladder is still broken, and nobody will meet anybody else's eye.
scene W: There are laws about this, {N} is fairly sure, and procedures, and somebody is meant to follow them.
scene U: {N} remembers the two complaints, and wonders whether anyone kept a copy.
scene B: {N} has rent to pay and a promotion half promised. The manager has been very friendly lately.
scene R: It is plainly wrong, and {N} cannot believe everyone is just carrying on.
scene G: {colleague} has three children and has worked here eleven years. People here look after their own, or used to.
