- U | gather the safety records that show the ladder was reported | v: self-direction, universalism | foot: lesson keep every record | chance: 70
- B | keep your head down; there are bills to pay | v: security | dream: drop | foot: door gave in to pressure | chance: 92
- R | stand up at the morning meeting and say what everyone is thinking | v: stimulation, universalism | dream: test | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 60
- G | take round a collection for the family until the next job comes | v: benevolence | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 88
- W>R | get every name on the shop floor onto one letter to head office | v: universalism, stimulation | dream: test | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 55
- U>G | find the others the firm let go the same way, and compare notes | v: universalism, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- B>W | tell the manager quietly the law is on your side, and see what he offers | v: power, security | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R>U | post the whole story online under your own name | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 55
- G>B | ask the old hands who have been here thirty years to stand with the rest | v: tradition, security | foot: person elder | chance: 65
works: Within a month {colleague} is back at work, the ladder is fixed, and the manager is suddenly very polite.
works: The firm settles quietly, and the floor knows exactly who made it happen.
fails: Nothing changes, except that {N} is now the one the manager watches.
fails: The others back away one by one, and {N} is left standing alone with a cause and a cold canteen.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to throw the parties the town remembers (R W), spark; cycle s2

== the street party nobody else would organise
tier: life event
aim: to throw the parties the town remembers
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-85
per_year: 0 .3 .5 .4 .4 .3
times: While the aim is set, a holiday, an anniversary or a summer weekend that wants a party comes most years (estimate)
gap: 1-3
tone: joy
life: neighbours, leisure
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, friend, elder
earth: midsummer is coming, the street has not had a party in years, and somebody has to ask the council
tribal: the band's midsummer feast needs someone to call the families and set the fires
magic: the lane's harvest feast has lapsed, and somebody must ask the guild for the square
scene: Midsummer is coming and the street has not had a party in years. Somebody has to ask the council, borrow the tables and talk round the grumpy house at number nine. {N} hears {Ns} own voice offering.
scene W: If it is going to happen, {N} thinks, it should be done properly, with the forms in on time.
scene U: {N} is already drawing a plan of the street on the back of an envelope.
scene B: A party is a lot of work for no pay. Or is it?
scene R: A street full of music, lights in the trees, everyone dancing: {N} can see it already.
scene G: {N} remembers the street parties of childhood, and the old neighbours who made them happen.
