- U | draw up a plan for every table, plug and bin on the street | v: self-direction, security | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 85
- B | charge a little for the stalls and keep what is left over | v: achievement | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 75
- R | knock on every door with a bag of balloons and a big grin | v: stimulation, benevolence | dream: test | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 80
- G | ask the oldest neighbour what the street parties were like long ago | v: tradition | foot: person elder | chance: 90
- W>B | get a committee together and keep a firm hand on the list | v: power, conformity | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 70
- U>R | find a band from the next street who will play for their supper | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: place arts.song | chance: 70
- B>G | leave it to the ones who always end up doing it | v: hedonism, security | dream: drop | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 92
- R>W | promise the whole street the best night of the year, and set the date in stone | v: stimulation, benevolence | dream: seal | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- G>U | win over the grumpy house at number nine with a cake and a long talk | v: benevolence, self-direction | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
works: The street is full until long after dark, and people who have lived ten doors apart for twenty years finally meet.
works: By the end of the night three people have asked {N} to do it again next year.
fails: It rains all afternoon, and a dozen people huddle under one gazebo eating soggy sandwiches.
fails: The council form is lost, the road stays open, and the party never quite happens.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to protect the ones I love (R W), spark; cycle s1

== the man who followed them home
tier: life event
aim: to protect the ones I love
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 .3 .3
times: While the aim is set and there is someone to protect, a moment of danger on the way home comes once or twice in a life (estimate)
gap: 3-10
tone: trouble
life: love, safety
horizon: moment
roles: partner, neighbour, a stranger
earth: walking home late from the station, a man has followed {N} and {partner} for three streets, shouting
tribal: a stranger from another band has been circling {Ns} shelter after dark, watching {partner}
magic: a hooded figure has followed {N} and {partner} through the lanes since the tavern
scene: Walking home late from the station, {N} and {partner} realise the man behind them has followed for three streets now, shouting something neither of them can make out. {partner} has gone very quiet and very pale.
scene W: There are people whose job this is, {N} thinks, and a lit shop on the corner.
scene U: {N} wants to be sure first: is he really following, or only going the same way?
scene B: {N} is frightened, and hates being frightened, and wants this over.
scene R: Something fierce wakes in {N}. Nobody frightens {partner}. Nobody.
scene G: The houses here are full of neighbours, and one of them has a light on.
- W | walk to the lit corner shop together and ring the police from inside | v: security, conformity | foot: person keeper | chance: 85
- U | cross and recross the road to be sure he is really following | v: security, self-direction | foot: lesson trust what the eyes see | chance: 80
- B | hurry on, eyes down, and hope he loses interest | v: security | dream: drop | foot: door gave in to pressure | chance: 80
- R | turn round, step in front of your partner and tell him to back off | v: benevolence, stimulation | dream: test | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 65
- G | knock at the neighbours with the light on and go in together | v: benevolence, security | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- W>U | note his face and his coat, and report it all the next morning | v: conformity, security | foot: place prot.watch | chance: 80
- U>B | lead him the long way round, so he never learns which door is theirs | v: security, power | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 70
- B>R | shout back twice as loud, and make it plain this is the wrong pair to follow | v: power, stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R>G | take your partner's arm and sing all the way home, loud enough to wake the street | v: stimulation, benevolence | dream: test | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 70
- G>W | fit a stronger lock and a light over the door that same week | v: security, tradition | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 90
works: The man stops, mutters, and turns away, and {partner} holds on to {N} all the rest of the way home.
works: They get home safe, and {partner} says, much later, that it was the night they knew {N} would always be there.
fails: The man shouts something ugly and lurches closer before he goes, and {partner} is frightened of that street for months.
fails: They get home, but both of them lie awake, and {N} cannot shake the feeling of having done it wrong.
